===Etymology===
From {{der|en|enm|bothe}}, {{m|enm|boþe}}, from {{inh|en|ang|[[bā]] [[þā]]|t=both the; both those}} and possibly reinforced by {{der|en|non|báðir}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*bai}}. Cognate with {{cog|stq|bee|t=both}}, {{cog|fy|beide|t=both}}, {{cog|nl|beide||both}}, {{cog|de|beide||both}}, {{cog|sv|både}}, {{m|sv|båda}}, {{cog|da|både}}, {{cog|no|både}}, {{cog|is|báðir}}. Replaced {{m+|enm|bō}}, from {{cog|ang|bā}}, a form of {{cog|ang|bēġen}}. A remnant of the Indo-European [[w:Dual (grammatical number)|dual grammatical number]].

