====Usage notes====
"'''''The'' both'''" is a colloquial and regional construction {{defdate|since 1843|ref={{R:OED Online|id=4133118075}}}} that imparts a sense of togetherness between the two people/things being mentioned. "''I saw '''both''' of them.''" can mean the two people/things were seen separately, whereas "''I saw '''the both''' of them.''" generally implies both were seen together.

